    "type": "aumf",
    "subtype": "TKI2",
    "manufacturer": "NDSP",
    "note": "`scripts/audit_manifest.py --pack toneking` reports CANNOT VERIFY against this plugin, and that is correct rather than a bug: it publishes 96 controls with real ranges, but keeps its Audio Unit state as opaque bytes instead of a document, so a preset key cannot be written into it and no key can be tied to a control by experiment. Matching the two lists by name alone reaches 35 of 259 and is a guess."
  },
  "draft": true,
  "drafted_from": "Default.xml",
  "description": "DRAFT pack for Tone King Imperial MKII. Generated by scripts/bootstrap_pack.py from one preset, in the second Neural DSP preset encoding: 8-byte binary doubles inside PARAM records rather than text values under their own keys. Reading, editing and writing all work. Kinds are guesses; ranges and selector members are absent because neither can be inferred from a preset. ON RANGES: this plugin publishes them to its Audio Unit, but they cannot be attached to these keys with confidence -- see the note on `audio_unit`. Do not transcribe a range onto a key because the two names look alike; that is the guess this project keeps catching itself making. Fill them in one at a time, each with a `range_source` that says how it was checked.",
